From 4f2f06005e1d628858c2116f386f50c1d43a482c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 09:10:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath10k: use large BMI downloads for QCA9377 SDIO

Without WoWLAN mac80211 stops the device when the system suspends and
ath10k downloads the firmware again on resume. On QCA9377 over SDIO the
download of the firmware image with 256-byte BMI transfers takes 3.2 s
of the 3.5 s spent in wiphy_resume(), and the whole system resume, the
screen included, waits for it.

The ROM accepts 2048-byte transfers, as on QCA6174 over SDIO. Measured
on an SM-T580 (QCA9377 hw1.1, firmware WLAN.TF.1.1.1-00061):
wiphy_resume() goes from 3474 ms to 1248-1255 ms over ten suspend
cycles, each followed by a reconnection with working traffic.

---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/core.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/core.c
index 7c2939cbde..6b84a99167 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/core.c
@@ -656,6 +656,7 @@ static const struct ath10k_hw_params ath10k_hw_params_list[] = {
 		.num_wds_entries = 0x20,
 		.uart_pin_workaround = true,
 		.credit_size_workaround = true,
+		.bmi_large_size_download = true,
 		.dynamic_sar_support = false,
 		.hw_restart_disconnect = false,
 		.use_fw_tx_credits = true,
-- 
